AI: 
                              Root Cause Analysis                               

ShopApiDown alert is firing because the api deployment in the shop namespace has
0 available replicas.                                                           

                               Chain of Failures:                               

 1 Postgres database is failing - The postgres pod (postgres-594bbc787f-5nfb7)  
   is in CrashLoopBackOff with 9 restarts. Logs show:                           
                                                                                
    Error: Database is uninitialized and superuser password is not specified.   
    You must specify POSTGRES_PASSWORD to a non-empty value for the superuser.  
                                                                                
   The POSTGRES_PASSWORD environment variable is empty (not set to any value).  
 2 API pod cannot reach postgres - The api pod (api-5d46ddb744-4drng) is in     
   Error state with 9 restarts. Logs show:                                      
                                                                                
    api: waiting for database                                                   
    Tue Aug 18 07:07:19 UTC 2026 api: cannot reach postgres                     
                                                                                
   The API container runs a health check loop (nc -z -w 2 postgres 5432) that   
   exits with code 1 when it cannot connect to postgres.                        
 3 No available replicas - Because the API pod keeps crashing (exit code 1), it 
   never becomes ready, resulting in 0 available replicas and triggering the    
   alert.                                                                       

                                      Fix:                                      

Set the POSTGRES_PASSWORD environment variable in the postgres deployment to a  
non-empty value:                                                                

                                                                                
 kubectl set env deployment/postgres -n shop POSTGRES_PASSWORD=<your-password>  
                                                                                

Or update the deployment manifest to include a proper password (ideally from a  
Secret):                                                                        

                                                                                
 env:                                                                           
 - name: POSTGRES_PASSWORD                                                      
   valueFrom:                                                                   
     secretKeyRef:                                                              
       name: postgres-secret                                                    
       key: password                                                            
                                                                                

Once postgres starts successfully, the API pod will be able to connect and      
become available.                                                               
